  "rules": [
   "H1 headlines: Geist Mono Regular, Title Case, filled with a White (#FFFFFF) to Cyan (#00D2FF) gradient on dark backgrounds.",
   "Tighten kerning on large Geist Mono headlines; it is monospace, so spaces and punctuation look too wide at scale.",
   "Eyebrows: Geist Medium, UPPERCASE, placed above the headline.",
   "H2/subheads: Geist Normal, sentence case.",
   "Body copy: Geist Regular, sentence case, 150% line height.",
   "CTAs and button labels: Geist Mono Regular, UPPERCASE; use #000000 text on light or Cyan Spot buttons.",
   "Use primary colours for backgrounds, headlines, subheads, body copy, CTAs and icons.",
   "Use secondary colours only for background elements and illustrations, never for body text.",
   "Use tertiary colours only for small parts of illustrations or diagrams.",
   "Use gradients to add depth to backgrounds: Purple Spot→Dark Spot or Navy Spot→Dark Spot; Blurple Spot→Cyan Spot or Cyan Spot→Blue Spot for spot elements and illustrations.",
   "All text must reach at least 4.5:1 contrast with its background; do not set body text in Blurple, Purple or tertiary colours on Dark Spot.",
   "Use the white primary logo on dark slides and the black primary logo on light slides; use only approved artwork.",
   "Use the icon or stacked logo only when the primary logo does not fit; never use the app icon in place of the logo.",
   "Keep clear space around the logo equal to the height of the 'T' on all sides, with no text, images or graphics inside it.",
   "Never display the logo smaller than 25px tall.",
   "Never stretch, rotate, recolour, outline, add effects to, retype or resize parts of the logo, and never use the icon as the letter T.",
